```C
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

// Function to copy bytes from one location to another
void copyBytes(void* dest, const void* src, size_t n) {
    memcpy(dest, src, n);
}

// Function to get the length of a string
size_t getLength(const char* str) {
    return strlen(str);
}

int main() {
    const char* message = "Hello, World!"; // The source string
    char buffer[50]; // The destination array

    size_t numBytes = getLength(message) + 1; // Add 1 for the null character

    copyBytes(buffer, message, numBytes); // Copy bytes from message to buffer

    printf("The copied string is: %s\n", buffer); // Print the result

    return 0;
}
```
This program defines a `copyBytes` function that copies a given number of bytes from one memory location to another, and a `getLength` function that calculates the length of a null-terminated string. In the main function, we copy the contents of the message into the buffer using these functions, then print out the copied string.
']

