    if (fd == -1) {
        printf("Failed to create or open the file\n");
        return 1;
    } else {
        printf("Successfully created and opened the file\n");
        close(fd);  // Close the file after use
    }

    return 0;
}
```

This code creates a new file named "filename.txt" if it doesn't exist or truncates it to 0 bytes if it already exists, then opens the file for writing only and fails if the file already exists. After opening the file successfully, the program prints a success message. If the file could not be opened or created, it will print an error message instead.
']

